    "help": "You graded severity as Major (High). Now grade the likelihood of the CONSEQUENTIAL harm landing — misuse, further spread, fraud — not the likelihood of the breach (it already happened, and the disclosure itself is already priced into the severity grade). Map the level descriptions onto exposure evidence for THIS breach: Rare fits data that is unintelligible (encryption with keys intact), verified non-access — or a known, trusted recipient's confirmed deletion or return; the middle levels (Unlikely, Possible, Likely) fit access possible or confirmed with no evidence of use, scaled by who plausibly has it; Almost certain fits confirmed exfiltration or data already circulating or misused. Read the percentage aids over the whole period the data remains exploitable, not a fixed year. EDPB Guidelines 9/2022 walk the same factors. At Major severity, grade Rare only on VERIFIED assurance — intact encryption with keys confirmed uncompromised, or confirmed non-access — not on general confidence in your controls.",
